WEBVTT

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:28.430
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:28.430
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:28.430
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.600 --> 00:02:02.630
Chapter XIII

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:12.130
On January 5th
of Space Year 789...

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:17.030
...the body of Kefenhiller,
who had died suddenly...

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:23.260
...was buried, attended by Yang and Patorichev, at a public cemetary on Planet Masszitt.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.830
That old man...

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:36.240
I don't suppose he could have imagined that he'd be buried in a place like this...

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.280
...and have people like
us hold his funeral.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:57.400
The cause of his death is cardiac infarction,
but he may have had other previous illnesses.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:01.280
He seems to have died in his sleep, and probably suffered no pain.

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:03.130
I see.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:06.790
Are you his kin ?

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.700
No, we are...

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.310
This old gentleman had
defected from the Empire.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.750
Since he was a relatively
important person to the military...

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:19.480
...we were ordered by a higher authority to accompany him to Heinessen.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:24.360
So we are not authorized to decide the matter of his funeral ourselves.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:31.410
Then, for the time being, shall we take custody of his body in our "corpse accommodation camp" ?

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:33.780
Is there such a place ?

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:35.240
Yes.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.930
In a place like this...

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.840
...we often have deaths of unidentified people due to sudden illnesses or accidents.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:50.900
The old man...

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.620
...is going to a camp again.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.410
...is what happened.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:08.460
Can you help us ?

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.660
I see what you're saying, but during this season, the hotels are all booked, so...

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.130
If we can just avoid the
night dew, I won't complain.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.190
Let's see...

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.440
If you don't mind staying at the airport construction workers' lodging house, it's vacant at the moment.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.490
Everyone's gone home for vacation, so...

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.780
Lt. Commander, if you had
mentioned your name...

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.920
...I bet they would've broken their backs to give us a luxurious hotel room, but...

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:44.560
I don't like doing things like that.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:46.310
I'm sure.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.430
Anyway, I'll try to open
communications with Heinessen.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.080
No good.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.580
Both the National Defense Committee and the Joint Chiefs of Staff Office's...

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.930
...just have answering machines
and no one is answering the phones.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.760
How carefree of them.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.340
I wonder what they would do if the
enemy attacked us at a time like this.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:22.930
The front lines are
still operational, I'm sure.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.060
I'll ask a friend of mine.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.470
This is an answering
message of misfortune.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:35.680
If you hear this, you must immediately make phone calls to 50 houses.

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.560
And if you actually do it, you'll be even more unfortunate.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.750
Goodbye for now.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:47.130
As always, you have
poor taste in humor.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:50.630
I'm having a little
trouble on my way back.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:52.380
Please give me a call when you return.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.670
I can be contacted at...

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:01.210
Commander Cazellnu is
really good at his job.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:06.560
Only a day after he got the
message, the burial is all set.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:08.730
Yes, he is.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.080
What about his personal effects ?

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:15.480
It's decided that I'm responsible for carrying them to Heinessen.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:19.760
A portion of them will be sent
back to his home via Phezzan...

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:24.790
...but it seems documents of any importance will be filed at the military public document archive.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:30.560
I wonder what the old
man thinks of that decision.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:33.760
We're finished.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.150
Is everything okay ?

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:50.150
"Christoph von Kefenhiller,
Imperial Year 408 to 480."

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:53.510
"In his lifetime, he saved
the lives of a few people."

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.210
Lt. Commander, did you...{write this}?

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:02.000
For someone like me
to choose his epitaph...

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.790
I wonder what that
old gentleman thinks of it.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:08.020
Well, I think he's happy with that.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:11.270
I wonder.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:28.180
One thing that's for sure is that because we
used the Empire's language for the epitaph...

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:31.680
...it cost us an extra 150 dinars.

00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:47.190
Come to think of it, I wonder if they're still alive, the Captain's wife and her lover ?

00:07:54.220 --> 00:08:00.420
Yang and Patorichev were finally able to leave
 Planet Masszitt on the following day, January 6th.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:03.760
It was an unexpected one week stay.

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:13.510
On January 28th, they finally arrived at the capital planet of Heinessen.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:28.030
Ordinarily, the journey does not take this long, but because of the stay at Masszitt...

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:34.830
...the schedule was significantly delayed for
things like no vacant seats on direct flights...

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:37.340
...or flights being canceled for
inclement flight route conditions.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.460
Thank you for all your trouble, Lieutenant.

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:57.430
Well, the gratitude is mutual.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:02.320
It'll be nice if we can work
together again in the future.

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:17.520
So long.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:25.750
Welcome home, Senior.

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:31.730
Oh, you came to pick me up.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:35.840
I'm sure you're disappointed that a man came, but I was ordered here by Senior Cazellnu.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.360
Senior Cazellnu is waiting for you, preparing a dinner party in recognition of your service.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:44.250
Well, it'll be March Rabbit again, or maybe Whitestock, with a bit more generosity ?

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:48.510
No, it seems like it'll be
home-cooking at his official residence.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:50.440
Home-cooking ?

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:53.570
I see, it's time for the
introduction of his fiancée, is it ?

00:09:54.210 --> 00:10:00.080
Yes, Senior Cazellnu moved to a new residence because of it, in preparation for his marriage.

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:05.760
Therefore, I came to pick you up as your guide to his new residence.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:07.730
Hop in.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.630
Senior Cazellnu's fiancée is his superior's daughter, right ?

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.690
Huh ? No, that's
not quite accurate.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:32.390
The correct way to put it would be that she was the daughter of someone who used to be his superior.

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:33.680
"Used to be" ?

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:39.200
Yeah, he{i.e. the fianc's father} is long since retired and is now Secretary of the Veterans Association.

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:42.680
I'm glad to hear that.

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:49.430
I never believed Senior Cazellnu would marry a superior's daughter for the sake of promotion.

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:50.990
Of course not.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:53.720
By the way, how's
the military academy ?

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.240
Has it changed at all ?

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:58.900
It wouldn't change
in just a year or so.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:03.380
Of the students and instructors, I like half of them and hate the other half.

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:08.080
Oh, that nagging Instructor Dawson was finally transferred out of there.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:12.830
Oh, that must be
good news for you.

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:16.780
It's not good news at all.

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:18.810
He's transferring at the
same time I graduate.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:22.390
If he's assigned to the same department I am
and is waiting for me with his usual arrogance...

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:26.130
...my soldier's life will
begin in utter darkness.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:28.590
It depends on how you look at it.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:31.830
It's better to start in darkness
than to end in darkness.

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:37.000
You're right, but if a bastard like
Dawson continues to get promoted...

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.250
...that'll be a misfortune
for the Alliance Forces.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.800
Even during an enemy attack...

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:46.420
...he'll be worrying about caloric miscalculations of soldiers' rations at the decimal level.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:50.470
It's scary just to imagine
fighting under his command.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:56.830
If you get promoted faster and become his superior to slave-drive him, everything will be just fine.

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:59.490
If you worry about something like
that now, you'll just get exhausted.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.160
Promotion, huh ?

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.620
With people like Dawson
are getting promoted...

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:07.070
...and the Alliance Force is in such
a state, I wonder how it{i.e. promotion} will turn out.

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:08.660
You shouldn't be so pessimistic.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.880
Even someone like me
got to be a Lt. Commander.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:15.230
You have more aptitude as a military officer than I do, so you'll be fine.

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:18.020
Please don't flatter me.

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:23.760
No, I mean, you did great when we
tag-teamed in a strategic simulation once.

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:29.390
No one can match your skills, especially when withdrawing from a lost battle...

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.830
...and exhausting the pursuing opposition while retreating.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.360
I remember it very well.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.830
I don't feel like
I'm being complimented.

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:38.020
Is that so ?

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:43.040
Well, no matter, as long as you don't rebel
against authority too much, you should be fine.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:48.530
With your talent, you shouldn't
have to count on a fluke, like I did.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:53.370
Hitting my superior and ending up in the brig would be more like it.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:57.820
I was brought up listening to the military being disparaged, so when I see an arrogant superior...

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:01.650
...I can't help but be rebellious.

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:02.850
Disparaged ?

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:03.750
By whom ?

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:04.740
By my father.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.290
By your father ?

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:07.790
What does he do ?

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:08.830
He's a journalist.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:13.960
I remember, you wanted
to be a journalist, too.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:18.730
From the perspective of a journalist, you can
see a lot of the ills in the military organization.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.530
Well, that's what I thought, too.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:29.030
But my father is the one who advised me to go to the military academy.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:34.980
Why are you sending me
to the military academy ?

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.590
You've always said nasty
things about the military !

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:40.540
Son, listen to me carefully.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:43.760
There's a profound reason behind this.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:47.080
When I wanted to
marry your mother...

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:51.980
...your mother's father, in other words your grandfather, absolutely opposed it.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:55.630
He was a hard-headed professional soldier...

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:59.250
...and he said he'd never let his
daughter marry anyone but a soldier.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.260
That's...

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:02.050
Listen first.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:06.030
After more than a hundred
quarrels and three fist-fights...

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:09.130
...I finally persuaded him to
let me marry your mother.

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.680
How nice.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:14.030
But he proposed one condition.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:18.930
That is, if we had a boy child, we'd make him a soldier.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:23.800
But the children
we had were all girls.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:31.450
Despondent over that, your grandfather died in a battle with the Empire just before his retirement.

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:35.880
Ten months later,
we finally had our first boy.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:40.930
We believed the boy was your grandfather's reincarnation, and gave him the same name.

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:43.120
That was you, Dusty !

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.030
What do you mean,
"that was you" ?

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:49.820
Well, it was basically his dying wish.

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:56.990
If he was still alive I could fight it, but since he's dead, there's nothing I can do.

00:14:56.990 --> 00:15:01.060
So your grandfather's spirit can rest in peace, join the military, Dusty !

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:02.560
Wait a minute !

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:09.120
So you were willing to sacrifice a child from the time of his birth in pursuit of your own happiness ?

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:12.280
Well, I guess you
can phrase it like that.

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:14.190
How else can you phrase it ?

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:15.830
What kind of a parent are you ?

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:17.870
Nothing will ever make
me become a soldier !

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:22.230
If you say things like that, your
grandfather will haunt you as a ghost.

00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:24.520
If he's going to haunt someone, it's you.

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:27.860
There's no reason I should
be haunted or cursed.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:36.230
Well, Dusty, have you no pity for the man who died with unrealized dreams and regrets ?

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:38.730
Then you should join the military !

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.620
This is not my problem !

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:45.960
Listen, Dusty.

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:51.940
If you refuse to join the military, your dead
grandfather and your parents will all be sorry.

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:55.830
But if you join the military,
in exchange for your unhappiness...

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:58.620
...everyone else around
you will all be happy.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:02.330
On the balance, it'll be a huge
plus in the end, and all will be well.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:06.490
Why can't you understand
such rational logic ?

00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:08.330
How can I understand it ?

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:17.330
Dusty, when did you 
become such a heartless soul ?

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:18.790
Your father is very very sad...

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.630
Cut it out.  Don't
pretend like you're crying !

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:22.030
Don't be such a bother...

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:29.950
In the end, we reached a compromise that I would apply to both the military academy and universities.

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:35.500
Unfortunately, I was admitted by the military
academy but turned down by the universities.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:38.300
So I reluctantly entered
the military academy...

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:43.000
...but my father is still writing
disparaging articles about the military.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:44.740
How egotistical.

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:48.400
Well, even if you went to a university, there's still the draft.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.830
Besides, if you hate it so
much, you can just retire.

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:56.470
You're right, but
there's an epilogue.

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:58.130
Huh ?

00:16:59.350 --> 00:17:04.540
This is what my father gave me as a "lucky charm," when I entered the military academy.

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:10.250
What's its benefit to me ?

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:15.040
That's what I was given at my
wedding by the father of my bride.

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:18.040
You mean Grandfather Dusty ?

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:19.570
Yes.

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:23.360
According to Grandfather, it's a 
good-luck charm of miraculous virtue...

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:27.730
...and because of this key,
his life was saved many times.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:28.570
Is that right ?

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:34.500
At one time, when he kept it in his chest pocket, it caught a bullet.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.900
I can't see any trace of a bullet.

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:39.450
Don't say such sinful things !

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:45.660
Just the other day, I wished for you to fail your university exams, and that wish actually came true !

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.130
Don't even think about
doubting its power !

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.430
What did you say,
you waste of a father ?!

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:55.900
He's really an atrocious father.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.390
Every time I go home,
we always quarrel.

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:03.690
He's more loathsome than
the faceless Imperial soldiers.

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:09.180
But your father's right: because he's alive, you can quarrel.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:13.620
In my case, I can only
gripe at the gravestone.

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:20.030
Um, I'm sorry, Senior, to have said such insensitive things.

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.550
No, don't worry about it.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:23.080
I was just a little envious.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:29.330
Well, it's not something
you should be envious of.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.630
I think it is.

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:36.680
After all, your aspiration to become a journalist is due to your father's influence, isn't it ?

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:40.870
Well, I'm reluctant to admit it, but...

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:44.020
So, that key - has it
brought you any divine favors ?

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:47.480
When I was new to the academy, I once broke curfew.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:55.100
As I was holding this key, the upperclassman on
watch duty pretended not to have noticed me.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:58.040
Huh ? Yeah, something like
that happened, didn't it ?

00:18:58.040 --> 00:19:00.780
Come to think of it, that was when you and I met for the first time.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:06.340
Maybe it's not a lie after all, that it's a key that brings about good fortune.

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:07.450
I don't know about that.

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:10.820
"Father"...

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:17.290
When things settle down, maybe I'll go visit his grave, as it's been a long time.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:30.490
This is Miss Hortance Milbelle.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:39.670
Um...she'll soon be "Mrs. Cazellnu."

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:44.480
I've heard you've been helpful to Alex.

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:46.130
Thank you.

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:49.290
And please come visit us
after we get married, too.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.350
Um...yes...thank you...

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:55.840
I...I'm Yang Wenli...

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.900
I'm Dusty Attenborough.

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:00.180
The two seniors have
been so helpful to me.

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:02.500
Um...I'm sorry.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:05.830
Since we came directly from the airport, we've come without bringing anything...

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:07.690
You don't have to be courteous, just be your usual self.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:09.420
This dinner party is for you today.

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:11.330
Besides, you've got many
stories to tell as souvenirs.

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:15.380
Wow, it smells delicious.

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:16.850
We've prepared it for you.

00:20:16.850 --> 00:20:17.870
Come in please.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:20.800
Hortance is rather good at cooking.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:27.580
Cazellnu's characterization was a modest one.

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:31.460
Yang and Attenborough
are far from gourmands.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:34.480
They've been in the military or
military academy for a long time...

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:39.980
...and they are so influenced by the philosophy that food is for filling the empty stomach...

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:43.010
...that their taste might
have become primitive.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:46.980
This was a dinner that
provoked such thoughts.

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:50.210
You like the stew, don't you ?

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:51.650
It's my favorite, since today.

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:56.140
The faster one wins.

00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:59.340
You're not deferring to your senior.

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:01.530
Besides, today's dinner party is for whom ?

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:03.080
Well, I'm hitting a growth
spurt and I need lots of food.

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:06.610
Also, there's no such thing as
"senior/junior" in the world of food.

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:19.530
Okay, so let's hear your story.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:22.300
Shall I remove myself
from the table for a while ?

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:24.810
Don't be so courteous,
unlike your usual self.

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:27.640
So, what are the
details you've uncovered ?

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:37.380
First, this is not
something I discovered.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:40.230
It's something Captain Kefenhiller
investigated and analyzed.

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:46.210
I must state that I only reconstructed his analysis from my perspective.

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:47.140
Okay.

00:21:50.130 --> 00:21:55.480
To start from the conclusion, Kefenhiller seems to think that Siegmeister and Michaelsen...

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:59.170
...constructed an espionage network within the Galactic Empire...

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:05.390
...and Bruce Ashbey used the information gleaned from that network to lead himself to many victories.

00:22:11.980 --> 00:22:15.740
But why would two admirals from the Imperial side do something like that ?

00:22:15.740 --> 00:22:17.580
For their own beliefs ?

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:22.810
Did they sympathize with republican democracy and betray their country for that reason ?

00:22:25.980 --> 00:22:29.050
That seems to be the case for Siegmeister.

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:39.190
The distant beginning of all this may lie in the fact that a man named Martin Otto von Siegmeister...

00:22:39.190 --> 00:22:45.850
...was born the son of a Department of Public Order Maintenance bureaucrat, in the Ministry of the Interior.

00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:48.480
Expressing it is difficult...

00:22:48.480 --> 00:22:52.710
...yet while realizing that difficulty, Yang
began to narrate the order of events.

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:59.030
Siegmeister and Michaelsen,
Bruce Ashbey and the 730 Mafia...

00:22:59.030 --> 00:23:02.340
Their connections were
about to be disclosed.

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:04.540
The End of One Journey

